// @check
// @error a `for` range counts in i32, so i32 and f64 bounds have no step — count with an integer and scale: `for i in 0 to 10 { const x = i / 10.0 }`
// A FLOAT bound is refused by its own sentence rather than the generic one, because it is the
// bound an author writes on purpose and the fix is a spelling they can act on. What the
// language owes a float range is a ruling, not a build: `open-rulings.md` §B8-for-float-range.
for i in 0 to 1.5 {}
